{ In this rosette, the kings are adjacent to each other. This is the non-cutoff type, because the white queen does not cut off the black king from the rook, and the black rook does not cut off the white king from the black king.
In all non-cutoff adjacent rosettes, white plays the same idea: to attack the rook from an adjacent square. }
1. Qc5+ Ke6 2. Ke4 Kd7 3. Qb5+ { Best for white is to give check from the pseudo-thorn position. } 3... Kc7 4. Ke5 Rg6 5. Qc4+ Rc6 6. Qb4 Rh6 7. Qe7+ Kc6 8. Qe8+ Kc7 9. Kd5 Rd6+ 10. Kc5 Rd7 { pseudo-Euwe position } *


