{ This is an adjacent rosette, cutoff type. The white queen cuts off the black king from the black rook, and the black rook cuts of the white king from the black king.
There is one plan that works well for white in most situations, and the two exceptions are for clear and obvious reasons. The best plan is to drive the black king towards the rook on the horizontal. }
1. Qg6+ Kd5 2. Qe4+ Kd6 3. Qd4+ Rd5 4. Qf6+ Kc5 5. Ke4 { Thorn position } 5... Rd7 { Black creates the same rosette again. } 6. Qc3+ Kd6 7. Qe5+ Kc6 8. Qe6+ Rd6 9. Qc4+ Kd7 10. Ke5 { Thorn position } 10... Rb6 11. Qf7+ Kc6 12. Qd5+ Kc7 13. Qc5+ Rc6 14. Qe7+ Kb6 15. Kd5 { Thorn position } 15... Rc8 16. Qb4+ Kc7 17. Qd6+ Kb7 18. Qd7+ Rc7 19. Qb5+ Kc8 20. Kd6 Rg7 21. Qf5+ Kb7 22. Qe4+ Kb8 23. Kc6 Rb7 24. Qe8+ Ka7 25. Qd8 { Philidor position } *


