1. Qg6+ Ke7 { Black's third option is Ke7. } 2. Ke4 { Again, approach the rook with the king. } 2... Rb5 { Maintaining the 4th rank cut-off, and eyeing b1 for a harassment defense. } 3. Qc6 Rb1 4. Qc3 Rh1 5. Kf4 { This is the most efficient move. The white king will attack the rook if it checks from the h file, and move to e5 if it checks from f1. } 5... Rf1+ 6. Ke5 { Black must return to a close defense. } 6... Rf7 7. Qc8 { Euwe position } *


