{ In this cutoff adjacent rosette, our key move Qa5+ would be possible. However, if our key would place the queen on or over the edge of the board, do not follow the main plan, because this pushes black towards the center of the board. In all such situations, look at the position of the black king. If it is not on the edge of the board, then play: }
1. Qd3 { attacking the rook with the queen. } 1... Rd4 2. Qc2+ Kd5 3. Qf5+ { Remember this pattern of checking first on the file, then on the rank. Now the black pieces are forced to separate. } 3... Kd6 4. Kc3 { Attack a hanging rook } *


