{ If the cage is on the 3rd rank, black has more options for his rook, but still no good king moves. The best option is still to drop the rook back to d6. Another option is to establish a 4th rank defense by moving the rook to g5. }
1... Rg5 (1... Rd6 2. Qg7 Rc6 3. Qg6+ Kd7 4. Qf7+ Kd6 5. Kd4 Rb6 6. Qf6+ Kc7 7. Qe7+ Kc6 8. Kc4 Rb7 9. Qe6+ Kc7 10. Kc5 Kd8 11. Qf5 Kc7 12. Qf3 Ra7 13. Qc6+ Kb8 14. Qe4 Kc7 15. Qe5+ Kb7 16. Kb5 Ra2) 2. Qc6+ Ke7 3. Qc3 Ke6 4. Qh3+ Kf6 5. Qh6+ Rg6 { White can give check with Qf4+ and proceed as for the third rank defense, but in the fourth rank case there is a quicker option, Qf8+, leading to Euwe in 2 moves. } 6. Qf8+ Kg5 7. Ke5 Kh5 8. Qh8+ Kg4 9. Qh7 Kg5 { Euwe } 10. Qh3 Rg7 11. Qg3+ Kh6 12. Qh4+ Kg6 13. Ke6 Rg8 14. Qe4+ Kg7 15. Ke7 *


