1. Qf4+ Ke7 { Creating the wishbone position with the black king on the second rank. In this position, attacking with the king is best. } 2. Kd5 Rg6 { Rosette } 3. Qc7+ Kf6 4. Qe5+ Kf7 5. Qf5+ Rf6 6. Qd7+ Kg6 7. Ke5 { We have repeated the thorn position, but one rank closer to the edge. As the pieces get closer to the edge, black's rook will have fewer squares safe from forks. } 7... Rf7 8. Qe6+ Kg7 9. Qg4+ Kh6 { Not a third rank defense, because the black king has no access to h4 or h5. } 10. Ke6 { Attack the hanging rook } 10... Rg7 11. Qh4+ Kg6 12. Qh8 { Euwe position } 12... Ra7 13. Qf6+ Kh5 14. Qf3+ { Check from the diagonal in front of the rook } 14... Kg6 15. Qg2+ Kh5 16. Qh1+ Kg4 17. Qg1+ { fork } 17... Kf3 18. Qxa7 *


