{ When it is possible for black to form this position, it is usually the longest distance to mate. White has three good options. When black is on the third rank, and the black king is at least as far from the edge as the rook is, then white's best way to play the body check position is to move to an Euwe position. }
1. Qb2 Rf3 2. Qb3+ Ke2 3. Qc2+ Ke3 4. Ke5 Rg3 5. Qc3+ Kf2 6. Qd2+ Kf3 7. Kf5 Rg2 { Since we are using the Euwe method on the third rank, at this point Rg2 is black's most effective defense. } 8. Qf4+ Ke2 9. Ke4 { taking opposition with the king } 9... Rf2 { Not the absolute best move (Rg8) this close to the edge. } 10. Qc1 { Euwe position } 10... Rg2 11. Qc2+ Kf1 12. Qd1+ Kf2 13. Kf4 Rh2 14. Qd4+ Kg2 15. Kg4 Rh7 16. Qe4+ Kf2 17. Qxh7 *


[Event "Queen vs Rook, Body Check: Chapter 2"]
[Date "2021.07.23"]
[Result "*"]
[Variant "Standard"]
[ECO "?"]
[Opening "?"]
[StudyName "Queen vs Rook, Body Check"]
[ChapterName "Chapter 2"]
[ChapterURL "https://lichess.org/study/jGkvtsxc/62hjt4wk"]
[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/methurst"]
[FEN "8/8/5rk1/8/5QK1/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[SetUp "1"]
[UTCDate "2021.07.23"]
[UTCTime "00:31:11"]

{ If the black king is very near to the edge of the board, then white is better off threatening to encircle black. }
