{ In corner defenses, white should place his queen on the main diagonal. }
1. Qd4 Rf7+ 2. Kg5 { With Kg5, white king controls f6, g6, and h6; white queen controls g7 and h8, so h7 and g8 are the black king's only squares. } 2... Rc7 { black adopts a distant defense } 3. Qe4+ { Queen gives check on the diagonal adjacent to the rook } 3... Kg8 4. Qe6+ { White gives check from the other diagonal adjacent to the black rook, and controls the checking square c6 so that the white king can move to f6 on the next move. } 4... Kh7 5. Kf6 Rg7 { Black's best defense is g7. } 6. Qe8 { Philidor } *


