{ White's main goal against corner defenses is to place his queen along the main diagonal controlling the corner square. }
1. Qe5 Rb7 { Best defense for black is a distance defense. } 2. Kg5 { White Kg5 controls f6, g6, and h6. White queen controls g7 and h8. Black king's only squares are g8 and h7. } 2... Ra7 3. Qe4+ { Queen gives check on the diagonal adjacent to the black rook } 3... Kg8 4. Qc4+ { Queen gives check on the other diagonal adjacent to the black rook and covers the checking square a6. } 4... Kh7 5. Kf6 { King moves to target square f6. } 5... Rg7 6. Qh4+ Kg8 7. Qh5 { Philidor } *


