{ With black to play it is possible to regroup, and black's position is fine. Black's most tenacious strategy in any rosette is to move toward the center. When already near the center, this usually means rejoining the rook with the king and attacking the opposing pieces.
White's best move is Kc3, creating a cage on d3. }
1... Rd4+ { And with best play black is 26 moves away from mate.
White's best move is now Kc3, creating a cage on d3. } 2. Kc3 Rf4 { Rf4 is not the most dilatory move, but effective and easy for the defender to remember. } 3. Qd3+ Kf2 4. Kd2 Rf3 { Body Check position } *


