{ In this position, white's best plan is always to play for an absolute seventh. }
1. Qa5 { Threatening Ke5 } 1... Kd7 2. Qb5+ Kc7 3. Ke5 Rg6 4. Qc4+ { Threatening a fork on f7 } 4... Rc6 5. Qb4 { Half-Philidor } 5... Rh6 6. Qe7+ { Black cannot maintain a 3rd rank defense because white controls both central squares. } 6... Kc6 7. Qe8+ Kc7 8. Kd5 Rd6+ 9. Kc5 Rd7 { Euwe position } 10. Qe5+ Kb7 11. Kb5 Rc7 12. Qe8 Rc1 13. Qe4+ Kc8 14. Kb6 Kd7 15. Qd3+ Ke6 16. Qe3+ Kd5 17. Qxc1 *


