1. Kd4 { Even away from the last rank, the absolute seventh position leaves black with only one move that doesn't lose quickly, retreating the rook. } 1... Rf5 (1... Kf5 2. Qf8+ Ke6 3. Qe8+ Kf5 4. Qxe5+) 2. Qe8+ Kf6 3. Ke4 Rg5 4. Qf8+ Kg6 5. Kf4 Kh7 6. Qd6 { Split the king and the rook. Note that the queen controls c5, d5, and e5 directly, and a5 and b5 indirectly, through forks from c7 and d7. } 6... Rg7 7. Kf5 { Moving the king one step closer } 7... Rf7+ 8. Ke6 Rg7 9. Qd3+ { Giving check and moving the queen to the long diagonal } 9... Kg8 10. Qd4 (10. Qd5 Rg6+ 11. Kf5+ Kh8 12. Qd3 Kh7 13. Qe4 { diagonal position }) 10... Rg6+ 11. Kf5 Rh6 12. Kg5 { Moving the king to attack the rook leaves it with no good squares } 12... Rh2 13. Qd8+ Kf7 14. Qc7+ Ke6 15. Qxh2 *


