{ White queen controls h5, one of the central squares on the 1st rank. }
1... Rf1 { Black moves his rook to a square opposite in color to that occupied by the white king. } 2. Ke4 { White moves his king directly in front of the black king, controlling f3, f4, and f5. } 2... Rf2 3. Qd6 { White queen now controls f6 and f8 directly, and f1 and f7 can be forked from g2 after checking on h2 and g6 after checking on h6, respectively. The black rook has no moves. } 3... Kg4 { Black's best defense is to move the king towards the center. } 4. Qd1+ Kg3 5. Qg1+ Rg2 6. Qe3+ Kh2 7. Kf4 { Aiming for the diagonal position } 7... Rg7 8. Qe5 Rg3 { Diagonal position } (8... Rg2 9. Kf3+ Kg1 10. Qa1+ Kh2 11. Qe1) 9. Qe4 { White triangulates to pass the move to black } 9... Rh3 (9... Rg7 10. Kf3 Rf7+ 11. Ke2 Kg3 12. Qg6+ Kf4 13. Qxf7+) 10. Qd5 Rg3 11. Qe5 Rg2 12. Kf3+ Kg1 13. Qa1+ Kh2 14. Qe1 { Philidor position } *


