{ From this position, black's best defense is Kg4, as we saw in the main line. An alternative, objectively less good, but perhaps catching the attacker by surprise, is Kh3. }
1... Kh3 2. Ke3 { Attack the hanging rook } 2... Rf1 3. Qd3 { Set up discovered check } 3... Rf6 4. Qc3 { Attack the rook } 4... Rg6 (4... Rf8 5. Ke2+ Kh2 6. Qc7+ Kh1 7. Qc6+ { two forking squares - fork next move wherever king goes } 7... Kh2 8. Qd6+ { fork } 8... Kh3 9. Qxf8) 5. Kf4+ { Give discovered check } 5... Kh2 6. Qc7 { Setting up the diagonal position with tempo. } (6. Qh8+ Kg2 7. Qe5 Kg1 8. Qc5+ Kf1 9. Qc1+ Ke2 10. Qc2+ Ke1 11. Qxg6) 6... Rg3 7. Qe5 { Diagonal position } 7... Rg2 8. Kf3+ Kg1 9. Qa1+ Kh2 10. Qe1 { Philidor position } *


