{ This is the Wishbone position. When the black king is on the edge of the board, white always follows the same winning procedure: }
1. Qh8+ Ke7 2. Kg6 { This is the thorn position, so called because of its resemblance to the old English character of that name. Note that white could have created a thorn on the first move, but when the king is on the edge checking with the queen first prevents the formation of a defensive rosette. At all other times, creating the thorn immediately is white's best move. } 2... Rf8 3. Qg7+ Ke8 4. Qc7 { Absolute seventh } *


