{ Javelin position on a central rank }
1... Rh3 { Prevents Qa3# } 2. Qd2+ { Give checks with the queen from the opposite side of the white king until you reach a position where h5 is covered, then move your king. } 2... Ka4 3. Qd1+ { Now the queen covers h5 and b3. } 3... Ka3 (3... Ka5 4. Kd5 Kb6 5. Qg1+ Kb7 6. Qg2 { set up discovered check } 6... Rh5+ 7. Kc4+ Ka7 8. Qg7+ Ka8 9. Qf8+ Ka7 10. Qf7+ { fork }) 4. Kb5 Kb2 { Give checks with the queen until black king is on a3 and h4 is covered. } 5. Qd4+ Ka2 6. Qd5+ Ka3 7. Qd6+ Kb2 8. Qf6+ { Queen now controls both h4 and c3. } 8... Ka3 9. Kc4 Ka2 10. Qf2+ Ka3 11. Qf1 { Queen threatens to capture rook and mate on a1... } 11... Rh4+ 12. Kc3 { And after king sidesteps check with a3, Queen also threatens mate on a5. Rook can't cover both mating threats. } 12... Ka2 13. Qf2+ { fork } 13... Ka3 14. Qxh4 *


