{ Even with one square between the king and queen, the javelin still works. While there is no mate threat, the king still shelters in front of the queen. }
1... Rc1 2. Qd4+ Kc8 3. Kd6 Rc7 4. Qf4 Ra7 { white offers a diagonal set-up } (4... Kb8 5. Qe5 { Diagonal } 5... Rb7 (5... Kb7 6. Qb5+ Kc8 7. Qa5 Rd7+ 8. Kc6 Rb7 9. Qa6 { pin } 9... Kd8 10. Qxb7) 6. Kc6+ Ka7 7. Qa1+ Kb8 8. Qa5 { Philidor }) 5. Qf8+ { If black declines to form diagonal, white gives pendulum checks on the eighth and seventh ranks and approaches the black king to threaten mate. } 5... Kb7 6. Qf7+ Ka8 7. Qe8+ Kb7 8. Qd7+ Kb8 9. Qd8+ Kb7 10. Qc7+ Ka6 11. Qc6+ Ka5 12. Kc5 Rc7 13. Qxc7+ { Even with one square between the king and queen, the javelin still works. While there is no mate threat, the king still shelters in front of the queen. } *


