{ This is not a Javelin, because the queen neither threatens mate nor shelters the white king from checks. Nevertheless, the tactics are the same, checking from a neighboring diagonal to create a fork and/or setting up a triple threat. }
1. Qc6+ Ke7 (1... Kd8 2. Qd5+ Ke7 3. Qd3 Kf7 4. Qc4+ Ke8 5. Kf6 { Bring your king closer, threatening mate on c8. } 5... Kd7 { Continuing checks from the neighboring diagonal would allow the king to shuttle between c7 and d8, so instead go for the triple threat. } 6. Qd3+ Ke8 7. Qc3 { Triple threat } 7... Rf1+ 8. Ke6 Kd8 9. Qd3+ Kc7 10. Qxf1) (1... Kf8 2. Qc4 { queen covers f1 } 2... Rb1 3. Ke5 Rb2 4. Kd5 Kf7 5. Kd6+ Kg6 6. Qe6+ Kh7 7. Qf7+ Kh6 8. Qf6+ Kh5 9. Qxb2) 2. Qc5+ Kd7 3. Qd4+ Ke8 4. Qa4+ Kf7 5. Qc4+ { Now white queen controls f1... } 5... Ke8 6. Kf6 Kd7 7. Qd3+ { and gives checks from the neighboring diagonal to the rook } 7... Ke8 8. Qb5+ Kd8 9. Qa5+ Kd7 10. Qxe1 *


