{ Let us return to our original position and explore another line of attack. }
1... Rh5 2. Ke4 Rh1 3. Qc7+ { This approach works reasonably well, and leads to the same zugzwang position } 3... Ke6 4. Qg3 { White has taken and simple and clear path to this position. However, black can shift his rook to the harassment diagonal and cause white some problems. } 4... Rb1 5. Qh3+ { White must first break the blockade of the king, before dealing with the rook. } 5... Ke7 6. Qc3 { White covers the checking squares b4 and e4... } 6... Rh1 { so black returns to h1. } 7. Kf4 Rh2 { Black tries again to hide on the white king's diagonal... } 8. Qg3 Rh7 { but white forces him to retreat to h7. } 9. Qg5+ Kf8 10. Qd8+ Kg7 11. Kg5 Kf7 12. Qd5+ Kg7 13. Qe4 Kg8 14. Kg6 Rg7+ 15. Kh6 { Diagonal cage } 15... Kf8 16. Qa8+ Kf7 17. Qb7+ { skewer } 17... Ke6 18. Kxg7 *


